  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Santiago Peña Palacios (born 16 November 1978) is a Paraguayan politician and economist who served as the 52nd president of Paraguay from 2023 until his arrest, dismissal, and prosecution in 2026. Peña served on leadership boards for the Central Bank of Paraguay and Banco Amambay. He taught economics at the Catholic University of Asunción.\nPeña is a former member of the Board of Directors of the Central Bank of Paraguay, and former minister of Finance of Paraguay. He was a member of the Authentic Radical Liberal Party beginning in 1996, until 2016 when he joined the conservative Colorado Party. He stood as a candidate in the Colorado Party's presidential primary in 2018, where he lost to Mario Abdo Benítez, who went on to be elected president in the 2018 general election. He later won the party's nomination for president in the 2023 general election, in which he ultimately won. \nHis government combined economic orthodoxy, social conservatism summed up in the formula \"pro-life and pro-family,\" and a close alignment with the United States.\nFollowing the political and financial crisis originating after the collapse of Ueno Bank, Peña submitted his resignation on 5 November 2026. Congress...",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
